{
  "id": "contrast-illusion",
  "term": "contrast illusion",
  "definition": "A contrast illusion is a perceptual effect in which nearby parts of a stimulus change how one part is seen, so that features such as brightness, color, or size appear different because of their context. In size-contrast forms such as the Ebbinghaus–Titchener illusion, surrounding elements can make a central object look larger or smaller than it would appear on its own.",
